<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44543" root="&#xA;                        ورى&#xA;                    " body-key="w1">
                        
                            <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَرَائِى كَذَا</span></b> 
                        
                        <i>Behind me is such a thing,</i> as
though it were a burden upon my back. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مِنْ</span>
                        <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَرَآءَ وَرَآءَ</span>
                        <i>From behind a thing covering,</i> or <i>concealing.</i> (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فُلَانٌ مِنْ وَرَآءِ فُلَانٍ</span>
                        <i>Such a
one is an aider of such a one:</i> or <i>a follower.</i>
(Ham, p. 206.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b4-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اَللّٰهُ مِنْ وَرَائِكَ</span>
                        <i>God is seeking after thee,</i> and <i>watching,</i> or <i>lying in wait,
for thee.</i> (Ham, p. 206.) See also an ex. in the
first paragraph of art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فتل</span>.

